      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T13:37:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Be wary of making too many assertions. It can lead to very brittle tests. Especially when picking a particular shade of a color. I\u0027d recommend sticking to very clear assertions of black/white where we can easily make a case that something should be fully covered or completely empty. I don\u0027t want to have to change this test if I slightly change how we linearly interpolate colors when blending or computing antialias.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 79,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "e897ceec282bdd0a4a584747977c7bb6c48f7177",
